data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":1717,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_039b606c04238855016acb4570b05c8193b5cfb372e0835433","object":"response","created_at":1791706480,"completed_at":1791706511,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_039b606c04238855016acb4571ac8c8193be8e32f048737469","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing tasks filter**\n\nI’m thinking about how to implement a server-rendered tasks filter that triggers on change. I need to make sure that when checkboxes change, the request submits while preserving the hidden filter. It’s important for this to be a reusable body helper, so it’s effective. I should also ensure that the existing body factor doesn't get disrupted. There’s enough time to make these edits properly, so I’ll focus on getting it right!"}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqy0V0ikl4oAOtTyLcigJIekXfh29OPts8tIVWer-pVYSaceY1KXVDa2ChZBf1yOByFei88-nJ31WrSq4rhYYRBF7IZBrS64MEmzwGCJcE8kXSRU_-BgEh0Di4s6iBRBdmAH8Y-TOzBEkpmQvlF_KfUFmRojV3TIeWID-g6jf0iF7D4yOQfWujfw78J7kQS5LZMG2KTLzRkHwj6N1zXtvWXdaflSMLe_j1uZeXmNxr-9c0A-KMnx54Z6FePUTGUq2jlT9KW8YNT7swp_T8Jj3o6a80fEDe1KY3xIleZXM2Dp35-yzdy1DL2cSsrdgIPD0tXEbo0uxS5ZcBXzdBZMTz8fkWyfH59GUgtIbhaR-Zq8xgaq37iJ8wwjGTqOvhFO1gW2GcglFsq-K-nu_XOGZC-51KaJxKRoideS0ss8VyVjPIPvHAEVhN1eA5DJWQkrtcp7HUtxecRaCyeqkn9IE2vXuPCVXuOVTjzbCPayRr9ybjJ2x5C177FXKsT7C6VTfD7pT6LTSWUH--8HhR0OUPlrjGEL_W37sePRr5A8WMJtxtXojUaw_asvrTYCthMsJSSC9fkWbxpMaPkR_t1DFtZOzFo0rzGt_nZVCB97s1Wqxqe5ME8D3X7fYQxs7Zb45cp8pWXEZKh5L5Fwz8M7Id5RyajITFWbVX1z-CugRpFeBkvWXUJuQhP2zB9_TzyNYfa6L6-X_oZime3M9sqbV_cWpk6-Jq7XfkjPRKMMRaYwbvtFt63SBhxfyt2Ez6n1OHWcR83BWKEazA6paW-WHafkUs8yuSBEw7Q0YIHJNC3pHHwhtoK2Br5gOVtbp5Z7sJiiPG1LNf3KBNvmweWhkS4wkHd8u0WplBoeyhgfojDoSDi1ckeKi49kSjGu4srP6eaj7pb4IKpFQmQT_Ae3y25xKzgQ6AE0TcNPr_tIv3_AbKnHoXMMUzpzxNTwYlnehJqGz0MQkc3aa7R75ljklh7Oq4nvuWikI8P8Dof38P6nP5IuTkqZeKNt2fW5wTlWyzCuGpVZtEkX-TBXbaXARI1q3NPgiArnw-jnSbGufPKvt41tRnDUYPv3_AiYLvtqcMtI4zWWt_tlAmaqCVCcoe7nqCETnP8htEPwTLsKccdSdjwcIcV2KePoVNldeLoUs-MhlrTMZOhxRmTDwgW0rjIkhcNrVcWsryn_yYhMl3LddR3gd-kf028KY6tKEtg0UDhzMjuXyHSJqpBYteTbQAN_k7s1qGRYo01weAOtHssjjDtYi7cmX1uYxcbpg9eUKW9pupfuSHBr7SXHUfTmu2Vrr3NOUsXIurmX2wKXXJZJ2tLB1bXDbenarVZZOF6TwNgBBk5CKHGoX05J2G3ixYpqmpo5pkW3quRbxiJ2CQ52bhQR8Z4-Ll76BNQARGldJbD-y9oL7SqZcgY0g5iz9YEzotdeeR05QCgc9JUb2ee4DrsxNzGbxwgSsqThG3WF2W7Li0ZrHbftDY5Lrm5UUm16ZPMgqrOPuSo5jQR3v7RZF_MBGq9PkHrjBt_y8EHjyquqFND3us1Vs9g7GXtrhMcsnuBzvoSzljcuvstQEVI5jHQcFhxNU0F2kj1VKU19FAefFTzsXBCKMFQzJI7bgOEFyOV5kkj3fR2noqE-EVzamYcwp_083ntcw0BqMQTbZX6UMVSo-t7vbwplfn5uLOEOcU8lyFNG0NpVtFKeZ9YN8FCVdpyHYa3bNuSzgfX0xTdxbHNdBGmewEAMrAm-LRHFN1zL752MB2OLizfZgBJ6WM8QfKc2xVUbqU6SiTYxvk2_j4DsZ8xP7Vz4Tfy0uss3aZUVnOJHRDyeCmeQSzynIxFSNfCMrpHwQtR4Avv51a7I8rk-C2DbsG34ri1H03u6aOzOjoIXGWJ-tzA_mvpmw3SgyYxgCJRV3supuUohONAMx72tw1z8gHcfHX0R8w9S32Cql